  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Calamine is the carbonate ore of zinc.It composition is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ZnCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>Galena is also called lead glance is the natural mineral form of lead (ii) sulfide,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PbS</mi></math></p><p>Sphalerite is a sulfide mineral with the formula<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ZnS</mi></math>.&nbsp;It is the most important ore of zinc.</p><p>Siderite&nbsp;is a mineral&nbsp;composed of iron(II) carbonate&nbsp;(FeCO<sub>3</sub>).</p>",
